WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:05.109
The One Piece Manga just revealed 3 shocking
things about Monkey D. Dragon, Vegapunk and

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:10.300
how a character we all believed to be dead
pretty much confirms the next destination

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.820
of the straw hats, the man with the burn marks
that kid is looking for.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.340
And since I chose to go with a Marine Admiral
Dragon for the Thumbnail, let’s start with

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.869
him and why this chapter might give credit
to that idea.

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:28.320
Oda just gave us the first proper flashback
for Luffy’s father, who has been even more

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.369
mysterious than characters like shanks.

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:35.540
We see Dragon, bringing a bouquet of flowers
to the chard and depressing ruins of the island

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:41.370
of Ohara, some time after the deadly buster
call had devastated the entire island and

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:42.370
all its people.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:48.500
Seeing a 22 year younger dragon is absolutely
awesome, he basically looks like Luffy with

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.489
long hair and Zoro’s personality.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:56.070
Interestingly enough, 22 years ago Dragon
doesn’t have his iconic tribal tattoo on

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.649
the left side of his face yet.

00:00:57.649 --> 00:01:03.070
Instead, you can see a very similar looking
pattern embroidered on his left pant leg.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:07.430
We also get confirmation that Dragon had just
founded the revolutionary army the very same

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.080
year the incident of Ohara happened.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.729
It seems that Vegapunk knew Professor Clover,
Robin’s father figure and the head archeologist

00:01:14.729 --> 00:01:16.000
of the island.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.700
I think this is a super interesting little
detail about Dragon’s past.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.820
He seems to have had real interest in the
void century and the past.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.040
We always suspected that Dragon would have
a decent amount of knowledge about the lost

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.630
history and the ancient kingdom, but the manga
has now pretty much confirmed this.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:37.869
Because this flashback is being told, not
from Dragon’s perspective, but from Dr.

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:38.869
Vegapunk’s.

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:44.920
Yes, the smartest person in One Piece was
on Ohara the very same day, also to lay down

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.549
a bouquet of flowers in memory of Ohara and
their work too.

00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:53.960
And yes, we finally get to see Dr. Vegapunk's
real appearance, and I will say, that this

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:59.580
mock artwork my team made for him a while
ago, did hold up surprisingly well.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:04.850
But we’ll get to that in a second, because
Vegapunk’s appearance holds a bunch of hints

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.880
and easter eggs that we need to discuss.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.690
Let’s stick with Dragon first.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.340
Now it was always hinted at that Vegapunk
might have ties to the revolutionary army.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.240
The biggest one of course being Kuma, whom
Vegapunk programmed to protect and save the

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.810
straw hats and watch over their ship during
the time skip.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.550
And while he isn’t an official member, we
do now know that Dragon actively tried to

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.510
recruit him to his cause.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:34.650
And while Vegapunk decided to work for the
government, apparently in order to get insider

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:40.489
information on their activities and plans,
Oda shows us that these two men seem to share

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:41.740
a common cause.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:47.200
Especially since we have seen Shaka in direct
communication with Dragon.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.870
What is really interesting here however, is
that despite their mutual liking and shared

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:55.240
cause, Vegapunk and Dragon didn’t come to
Ohara together.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:01.170
In fact, Vegapunk is extremely shocked to
see Dragon there, to which Dragon replies

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.630
that that’s his line.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:07.450
Both of them feel like the other shouldn’t
be on Ohara right now for some reason.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.879
Which brings me back to the thumbnail.

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:16.239
Could this meeting on Ohara be a hint at Dragon
being a former Marine or Cypher Pol agent?

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:20.120
After all, there are a lot of theories out
there about this.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:25.230
The world government making him the most wanted
person in the world and number one threat

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.360
to their rule.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.560
Going to such extremes as putting him over
people like Kaido and Big Mom suggests that

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.790
they know things about Dragon and what he’s
capable of.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:42.110
Monkey D. Garp being one of the biggest names
in the marines, who we know also tried to

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.620
recruit Luffy.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.180
Vegapunk comments how Dragon is someone who
despises war.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:51.829
And in this chapter we see another former
Marine who was chasing after the archeologists,

00:03:51.829 --> 00:03:54.650
only to try and save them in the end.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.250
Haguwar D. Saul.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:01.910
Who is actually confirmed to be alive and
well on Elbaf.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.269
We’ll also get to that part.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:09.349
Saul, just like Dragon is a member of the
D clan, who became disillusioned with the

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.349
government.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:15.470
And as we know Dragon doesn’t want to take
down the marines, but the celestial dragons,

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:19.880
which would make sense if he had a lot of
friends there.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.950
Overall there are a lot of arguments for and
against the possibility of Dragon being a

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.310
former Marine slash Cypher pole member.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:31.650
If that were true though, it would make a
lot of sense for Vegapunk to react the way

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:32.650
he does.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:38.750
If Dragon betrayed the government and founded
the revolutionaries, he should stay away from

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.740
an island that was burned to the ground for
its forbidden research.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:47.410
Dragon clearly learnt something about the
true history and the meaning of his D initial

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.300
from the archeologists.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:54.500
And he even says that he can’t have Dr.
Clovers death and the will of Ohara be in

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.500
vain.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.380
In other words, Dragon has inherited the will
of Ohara.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.960
Which you know, is pretty cool.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:06.570
Now a really interesting detail here hidden
in the japanese is that Dragon only founded

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:10.190
the revolutionary army AFTER this meeting
with Vegapunk.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:15.699
While Vegapunk is introduced as the head researcher
on Punk hazard, Dragon is not introduced as

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:22.500
supreme commander of the revolutionaries,
but as commanding officer of the liberation

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:28.289
or freedom army, an organization that we have
never heard of before in one piece.

00:05:28.289 --> 00:05:35.300
Maybe it’s an earlier version of the revolutionaries,
but it might also be something else entirely.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:40.319
What seems pretty apparent though, is that
the revolutionary army were a direct product

00:05:40.319 --> 00:05:41.780
of the Ohara incident.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:47.780
He decided, that he would do everything in
his power, until every last person in the

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.730
world is subscribed to the Ohara channel.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.910
But what really was Dragon’s connection
to the revolutionaries?

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:59.550
Now it’s plausible that Dragon was simply
affiliated with Clover and got all his information

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.180
about the world from them.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:07.690
However, I want to speculate here for a moment
if there might not be a bit more to it.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.340
You might know where I’m going with this.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:16.270
After all this chapter also heavily features
Nico Robin and her mother Olvia, quite a lot

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.270
actually.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:21.039
So let me just throw it out there: We don’t
know Robin’s father.

00:06:21.039 --> 00:06:25.880
We do know though, that he must have had black
hair, since Olvia’s is white.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:33.830
And I think it would make a ton of sense story
wise, if Dragon was actually Robin’s father.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:40.000
Think about it: Yes the incident of Ohara
was cruel and losing friends would make you

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.290
hate the government.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:46.590
But what would really make someone who hates
war like Dragon, suddenly form a militant

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:50.050
revolutionary group against the government
itself?

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:57.479
Well losing your woman and child to the governments
craziness surely would explain that.

00:06:57.479 --> 00:07:06.199
Plus laying down flowers The reason why the
gorosei targeted Ohara was because they captured

00:07:06.199 --> 00:07:08.580
Olvia and her comrades.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.669
Could they have targeted her because Dragon
left the government?

00:07:12.669 --> 00:07:16.990
Also remember that Dragon was incredibly interested
in meeting Robin and instructed Kuma with

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.380
sending her to him.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:22.770
The Revolutionaries who helped Robin at Tequila
Wolf, revealed that they had been searching

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:27.580
for her for ten years because she was the
only survivor from Ohara.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:33.180
Dragon, told them to protect her from the
World Government to the best of their abilities.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:39.260
Robin being Luffy’s half sister would be
an absolutely fantastic reveal in the story.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:42.830
Robin has truly been the older sister he never
had.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:47.930
But since there isn’t all too much evidence
for this, let’s put it aside for now and

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:50.629
instead focus on Vegapunk.

00:07:50.629 --> 00:07:55.180
We already discussed Vegapunk’s affiliation
with clover, who by the way is revealed as

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:02.650
an adventurer like Nolan in his youth, being
captured more than 10 times by the government.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:08.349
He dedicated his life to travelling around
the world and piecing together the void century.

00:08:08.349 --> 00:08:13.990
Now we finally also get to see what Vegapunk
actually looks like.

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:16.000
And it’s as Oda as it gets.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:21.910
Among the army of quirky characters he has
drawn so far, this is one to rule them all.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:24.530
I can never unsee this.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:27.470
Vegapunk seems to be part of the same race
that Fukurokuju belongs to.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:32.089
It is also the same head shape that we see
on the flag of the space pirates that enel

00:08:32.089 --> 00:08:33.089
encounters.

00:08:33.089 --> 00:08:38.330
And there is a lot of room for speculation
that Imu, due to their strange placement of

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:44.570
arms and the top of their head, might be part
of the same race as well.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:50.430
These people are all associated with extremely
high intelligence and technological advances

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:52.100
due to their large brain.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:58.720
And it seems that Vegapunk has since split
his brain into six parts, that he has infused

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:04.279
into the 3 robots and 3, i want to say people,
that are part of his persona.

00:09:04.279 --> 00:09:09.900
It also explains their personalities, as each
vegapunk has most likely inherited whatever

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.020
function the original brain part held.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:18.510
Now, I probably don't have to point this out,
but Vegpaunk is of course the spitting image

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:24.010
of Albert Einstein the genius german scientist
who developed the theory of relativity.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:30.430
Especially the most famous photo of him, where
he sticks out his tongue, resulting in a permanent

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:34.030
long tongue for the original vegapunk.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:39.630
Maybe this race has an elongated head, plus
something else, after all Fukurokuju has elongated

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.300
ear lobes.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:45.930
The brain split thing also fits into the Einstein
inspiration.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:53.079
After his death, Einstein’s brain was removed
and split into parts for further research.

00:09:53.079 --> 00:09:57.750
The fact that Vegapunk is covering up his
head with an apple is a nice little nod at

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:06.770
Issac Newton and the famous apple that fell
on his head, that made him discover gravity.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:11.399
It turns out, that Vegapunk didn’t only
reverse engineer the ancient kingdom’s technology

00:10:11.399 --> 00:10:13.260
from stuff he found lying around.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:21.029
It turns out that the scholars of Ohara actually
succeeded in rescuing the contents of the

00:10:21.029 --> 00:10:27.280
library from the fire, by throwing all the
books into the lake, sacrificing their lives

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.240
in the process.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:33.930
These books were then collected by the giants
of Elbaf, that due seem to be part of Hajrudin’s

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:36.580
crew if i’m not mistaken here.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:42.680
It looks like the giants of Elbaf are confirmed
as another ally of the ancient kingdom here,

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:46.899
next to Shandora and Wano.

00:10:46.899 --> 00:10:52.370
And it was here on Elbaf, that Vegapunk showed
his true genius.

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:58.959
He learnt all that knowledge in all the books
by heart and started to get to work, replicating

00:10:58.959 --> 00:11:00.220
its contents.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:04.590
In other words, everything that vegapunk knows
about the ancient kingdom and devil fruits,

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:09.510
it’s all thanks to the research of the archeologists
on Ohara.

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:12.370
They figured it all out by themselves.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.700
The real chads of One Piece in other words.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:20.860
SO Vegapunk is a real genius, just not in
the way we thought he would be.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:26.180
And he does seem to genuinely be a good guy,
that has been waiting for Luffy, though we’ll

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:28.410
have to wait and see about that.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:33.020
I’m sure there are still a ton of reveals
left during this arc.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:42.970
Though i do have the feeling that it might
be on the shorter end of things.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:49.050
So let’s finally talk about the person that
saved all the knowledge from Ohara and brought

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:52.780
it all to Elbaf: Hagwar D. Saul is alive.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:57.779
And so it seems that Aokiji hasn’t killed
a single person in the entire story.

00:11:57.779 --> 00:12:01.050
He froze Luffy and Robin, but made sure they
would survive.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:04.850
Same with Doflamingo and same with Saul as
it now turns out.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:11.540
He didn’t kill his friend, but instead probably
saved his life, with the ice saving him from

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.890
the flames.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:17.060
Another major hint, that Aokiji might be working
with Dragon to infiltrate Blackbeard.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:21.920
Now we don’t know if Saul got severely burned
by frost bite or by the fire of the buster

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:25.199
call, but he is alive.

00:12:25.199 --> 00:12:31.600
And seeing Robin’s tears of Joy after realizing
that, might be one of the most emotional panels

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.370
since the time skip in all of one piece.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.570
Really made me tear up.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:42.160
Now, given his burns, Saul sounds a lot like
the prime candidate right now for the man

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:48.529
marked by flames that Kid is looking for,
that has the last road poneglyph in his possession.

00:12:48.529 --> 00:12:55.260
That of course makes sense for two reasons:
One, Saul as the safekeeper of Ohara’s will,

00:12:55.260 --> 00:13:02.080
the only people who can read the poneglyphs,
would be a prime candidate to have it.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:05.330
It might even have been ON ohara originally.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:10.000
And two, we always speculated that it most
likely would be on Elbaf, an island that most

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.639
likely is under the protection of Shanks.

00:13:12.639 --> 00:13:17.779
That makes Elbaf 99,99% the next arc of One
Piece.

00:13:17.779 --> 00:13:22.610
And i discovered WHY Shanks is most likely
guarding the last poneglyph there and WHAT

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.120
will most likely happen during that arc.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.020
if you are curious, make sure to watch that
video right here next.

